1
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:16,016
Okay.

2
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:22,055
Anastomosis of vena cava and hepatic
vein has to be a continuous suture.

3
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:25,992
Stretch your suture gently.

4
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:30,063
No, no, no.
Use your finger, instead of forceps.

5
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:33,767
Interval of each suture
must be short, you know.

6
00:00:34,234 --> 00:00:37,337
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

7
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,607
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

8
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:43,209
<i>Medical care has become a world</i>

9
00:00:43,309 --> 00:00:46,946
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

10
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:50,650
<i>To save this crisis</i>
<i>in the world of medical care,</i>

11
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:55,955
<i>a freelance doctor, in the other words,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

12
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:58,992
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

13
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:01,861
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>

14
00:01:01,928 --> 00:01:03,096
<i>and being controlled.</i>

15
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:07,634
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

16
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:11,838
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

17
00:01:12,439 --> 00:01:15,375
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

18
00:01:20,146 --> 00:01:23,049
Welcome, Professor Kusakabe.

19
00:01:23,116 --> 00:01:24,050
Thank you. Hello.

20
00:01:26,152 --> 00:01:29,389
I can't be happier
seeing everyone welcoming me.

21
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:32,492
Of course. Welcome back, Kusakabe.

22
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:33,760
It's been a while, Hiruma.

23
00:01:34,627 --> 00:01:36,596
Good to see you again.

24
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:39,365
- Wonderful!
- We were waiting for you.

25
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:42,635
Thank you, thank you.

26
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,754
What a shady act.

27
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:05,191
- Come this way.
- It's been a while.

28
00:02:05,525 --> 00:02:06,526
Nice to meet you.

29
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:11,397
Professor Kusakabe. I'm Jonouchi.

30
00:02:13,032 --> 00:02:16,069
You're the one
who sent me a hot love letter.

31
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:21,040
Yes. I'm so honored to meet you.

32
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:24,344
Thank you.

33
00:02:25,378 --> 00:02:28,982
Even pretty flowers
look dull next to you though.

34
00:02:31,351 --> 00:02:33,019
You're so beautiful to me.

35
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:38,525
What?

36
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:39,859
Oh, let's go.

37
00:02:42,695 --> 00:02:44,063
You have not changed.

38
00:02:49,969 --> 00:02:51,638
Wake up.

39
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:04,951
Massachusetts Medical School

40
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,620
produces many Nobel laureates.

41
00:03:07,754 --> 00:03:09,722
Prof. Kusakabe is one of the best.

42
00:03:09,956 --> 00:03:12,125
It's like a divine spirit owns him
when he operates.

43
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:15,028
He's known worldwide as a doctor
who has "God's hands."

44
00:03:15,094 --> 00:03:18,932
I heard he was known as a genius
when he worked at our hospital.

45
00:03:19,966 --> 00:03:23,269
It's all thanks to you that

46
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:28,041
we could invite Professor Kusakabe
from the United States.

47
00:03:28,141 --> 00:03:31,644
Kusakabe's demonstration operation

48
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,881
will be broadcast live to
all university hospitals nationwide.

49
00:03:35,415 --> 00:03:40,286
I'm sure his skill
will be highly praised.

50
00:03:40,587 --> 00:03:42,255
KANEO KARASUMARU
OFFICE MANAGER

51
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:46,526
- This is like a dream.
- I invited him.

52
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,463
I can't wait to see
the techniques of a genius.

53
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:54,234
It's such a triumphant return.

54
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,902
I'm so proud that he worked here.

55
00:03:59,939 --> 00:04:03,409
Prof. Ebina and Prof. Kusakabe
were classmates.

56
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:05,044
I'll be careful.

57
00:04:11,451 --> 00:04:12,552
Can I come in?

58
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:14,654
Prof. Kusakabe.

59
00:04:21,961 --> 00:04:23,997
Here's a world famous doctor.

60
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:25,832
It takes me back.

61
00:04:26,499 --> 00:04:28,668
I'm walking around here.

62
00:04:29,302 --> 00:04:31,571
Nothing has changed here.

63
00:04:33,506 --> 00:04:36,242
When we were medical interns,
Ebina sat here.

64
00:04:37,143 --> 00:04:37,977
Yeah.

65
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:41,581
And I sat here.

66
00:04:41,881 --> 00:04:44,284
Oh, God.

67
00:04:44,484 --> 00:04:45,885
I'm so lucky.

68
00:04:46,019 --> 00:04:48,154
Prof. Kusakabe used to
sit where I sit now?

69
00:04:49,389 --> 00:04:52,158
They sat next to each other?

70
00:04:52,225 --> 00:04:54,527
Life can be cruel.

71
00:04:54,661 --> 00:04:56,696
I sit where Prof. Ebina used to sit.

72
00:04:57,764 --> 00:04:58,765
Move.

73
00:05:05,772 --> 00:05:07,607
I heard about you.

74
00:05:08,274 --> 00:05:12,745
You're the one who uses my phrase
without permission, Dr. Daimon.

75
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:16,182
- Phrase?
- "I never fail."

76
00:05:17,517 --> 00:05:21,220
I'm the first one to use it.
I own the right.

77
00:05:21,454 --> 00:05:24,257
Can you refrain
from using it from now on?

78
00:05:24,724 --> 00:05:25,625
What?

79
00:05:48,381 --> 00:05:49,816
Great.

80
00:05:50,883 --> 00:05:52,085
Here you go.

81
00:05:52,752 --> 00:05:56,723
However, you may use it

82
00:05:57,156 --> 00:05:58,558
if you pay homage to me.

83
00:05:59,258 --> 00:06:01,427
I won't refrain from using it.

84
00:06:02,795 --> 00:06:04,764
And I won't use it as homage to you.

85
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:06,366
Move.

86
00:06:10,103 --> 00:06:13,306
I didn't know
she just stole the phrase.

87
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:14,741
She's just a copycat.

88
00:06:19,145 --> 00:06:22,982
He's so shady. How can there be
a doctor who never fails?

89
00:06:23,449 --> 00:06:24,417
Except me.

90
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:27,987
Professor Kusakabe is not like you.

91
00:06:28,287 --> 00:06:29,455
You are captivated by him

92
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:31,457
- after being hugged.
- Hey...don't poke me.

93
00:06:31,524 --> 00:06:33,192
Don't say stupid things.

94
00:06:33,359 --> 00:06:36,896
Prof. Kusakabe is the only doctor
I can respect.

95
00:06:37,163 --> 00:06:38,698
Not only his skill,

96
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:41,968
the care he shows for the staff
and patients are first class.

97
00:06:42,168 --> 00:06:44,470
He was advertised on the cover of
<i>Time </i>magazine

98
00:06:44,537 --> 00:06:46,506
as a genius
nurtured by his own character.

99
00:06:46,639 --> 00:06:48,074
I saw that, too.

100
00:06:48,207 --> 00:06:50,009
The cover of <i>Time</i>? So what?

101
00:06:50,143 --> 00:06:52,111
So he's not like you.

102
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:54,147
Hey, stop arguing.

103
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:56,549
What did you write
in the love letter?

104
00:06:56,616 --> 00:07:01,521
I'm a single mom,
looking for a lover!

105
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:04,157
- Yes, she is!
- Mai.

106
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:10,129
I asked him if I could take part
in his operation as an anesthetist.

107
00:07:10,997 --> 00:07:14,233
Yuck!

108
00:07:14,534 --> 00:07:15,401
Listen.

109
00:07:15,535 --> 00:07:19,005
Prof. Kusakabe is the best doctor
in the world,

110
00:07:19,071 --> 00:07:22,942
and this is a rare chance
to join his operation.

111
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:24,177
So I made up my mind.

112
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:25,211
Hiromi.

113
00:07:25,645 --> 00:07:29,649
You got that job by yourself.
You're much better than Michiko.

114
00:07:29,715 --> 00:07:31,417
- But I'm not being paid.
- What?

115
00:07:31,484 --> 00:07:36,422
Many doctors would be willing to pay
just to be present at his operation.

116
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,558
That's not professional.

117
00:07:38,891 --> 00:07:40,793
I could never ask to be paid.

118
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,062
You should learn from Michiko.

119
00:07:43,362 --> 00:07:45,231
Why the change of attitude?

120
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:49,802
What kind of a smile is that?

121
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:53,840
Anyway,
it was a daring act of Hiruma.

122
00:07:53,906 --> 00:07:56,609
It must cost him a huge amount
to invite Kusakabe over.

123
00:07:57,410 --> 00:07:59,178
Is he that expensive?

124
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:02,315
Even if you add Hiromi's and your fees,

125
00:08:02,615 --> 00:08:05,518
and multiply that by 10,
his paycheck would be more than that.

126
00:08:05,585 --> 00:08:06,619
You're kidding.

127
00:08:06,752 --> 00:08:08,554
It's still a good deal for Hiruma.

128
00:08:09,222 --> 00:08:13,759
He invited a world famous doctor
before the chairperson election.

129
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:17,029
He'll be acknowledged
for his political skill.

130
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:19,799
And the outpatients will increase.

131
00:08:20,066 --> 00:08:24,437
But there are suspicions
towards his "no failure" record.

132
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:26,439
- Suspicions?
- Like what?

133
00:08:27,907 --> 00:08:32,245
I hear there is a trick behind
his 100% successful operation.

134
00:08:32,778 --> 00:08:35,481
- What do you mean?
- I don't know more than that.

135
00:08:38,317 --> 00:08:39,819
ICHIRO GOMI, AGE 50

136
00:08:42,088 --> 00:08:44,757
I call it an average man's jealousy.

137
00:08:44,824 --> 00:08:48,594
How could there
be a trick for God's hands?

138
00:08:49,595 --> 00:08:52,198
Well, you never know,

139
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:56,836
it could just be some sleight of hand.

140
00:08:56,969 --> 00:08:58,137
Ron!

141
00:08:59,472 --> 00:09:00,339
All Green!

142
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:02,174
Wow!

143
00:09:03,843 --> 00:09:05,244
You did a magic trick!

144
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:08,247
- Hello.
- I'm here to meet Kusakabe.

145
00:09:08,314 --> 00:09:09,315
Certainly.

146
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:13,986
- This way, please.
- Thanks.

147
00:09:15,621 --> 00:09:18,491
It took me longer than I thought
to draw a draft for the paper.

148
00:09:18,758 --> 00:09:19,625
That's alright.

149
00:09:19,825 --> 00:09:22,194
I'm still required to publish.

150
00:09:24,664 --> 00:09:28,734
Are those the candidates
for your demonstration operation?

151
00:09:29,869 --> 00:09:33,506
Yeah. I think I'll go with this patient.

152
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,543
- Esophageal cancer.
- It's stage three.

153
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:41,614
It's like you to choose the one
who needs the toughest surgery.

154
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,350
Others don't need to be me.

155
00:09:46,819 --> 00:09:49,755
"Don't need to be me?"
You haven't changed.

156
00:09:52,525 --> 00:09:53,759
You were always like that.

157
00:09:54,193 --> 00:09:57,129
"It doesn't have to be me."
"Only I can do it."

158
00:09:58,564 --> 00:10:00,333
You had your own standard.

159
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:05,838
Maybe that's why I couldn't
survive in an organization

160
00:10:06,072 --> 00:10:08,608
without causing trouble.

161
00:10:10,743 --> 00:10:13,112
I'm a loser.

162
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:14,680
Stop it.

163
00:10:15,815 --> 00:10:18,818
You couldn't adapt to a system
because you were a genius.

164
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:21,320
A genius can't mingle with the mediocre.

165
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:24,457
All your classmates knew that.

166
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:27,393
Nice to be with an old pal.

167
00:10:28,194 --> 00:10:30,429
He isn't shy to give compliments.

168
00:10:31,998 --> 00:10:33,766
- Here you are, sir.
- Thanks.

169
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:44,243
This is good.

170
00:10:48,514 --> 00:10:52,652
By the way,
about that female doctor, Daimon.

171
00:10:53,219 --> 00:10:56,055
- Daimon?
- What's her background?

172
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:01,460
I heard she's practiced medicine
around the world.

173
00:11:02,228 --> 00:11:03,963
But who knows...

174
00:11:05,564 --> 00:11:07,900
She repeats "I won't do it"
and "I never fail"

175
00:11:08,734 --> 00:11:11,237
and never gets tired of it.

176
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:14,740
She's just a stuck-up
and arrogant part-timer.

177
00:11:17,076 --> 00:11:17,977
I see.

178
00:11:19,545 --> 00:11:20,479
Why are you curious?

179
00:11:22,715 --> 00:11:24,350
I've met her before.

180
00:11:30,222 --> 00:11:32,558
A live demonstration operation?

181
00:11:33,325 --> 00:11:34,527
What's that?

182
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,328
It's an open operation.

183
00:11:36,462 --> 00:11:40,466
Your surgery will be broadcast live
to all hospitals and universities.

184
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:43,969
I don't want to make a show.

185
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:47,940
But a world famous doctor will
perform your operation.

186
00:11:48,074 --> 00:11:52,211
He's your surgeon, Prof. Kusakabe
of Massachusetts Medical School.

187
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:53,746
I'm Kusakabe.

188
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:57,016
He is a brilliant surgeon
known to have God's hands.

189
00:11:57,149 --> 00:11:58,718
That makes even less sense to me.

190
00:11:58,784 --> 00:12:00,086
I am the owner of a noodle shop.

191
00:12:00,152 --> 00:12:02,088
I can't afford to
have such a great doctor.

192
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:05,925
If you cooperate, this hospital
will pay for all your expenses.

193
00:12:06,692 --> 00:12:07,760
All expenses?

194
00:12:07,827 --> 00:12:10,529
This is a valuable operation
to the future of medicine.

195
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,567
My body is related to
the advance of medicine?

196
00:12:15,101 --> 00:12:16,001
Yes.

197
00:12:18,337 --> 00:12:20,005
What should I do?

198
00:12:20,106 --> 00:12:22,842
You should do it, Mr. Gomi.

199
00:12:23,008 --> 00:12:26,378
What luck to have a surgeon
operating with God's own hands.

200
00:12:27,012 --> 00:12:28,581
It's like winning a lottery.

201
00:12:28,814 --> 00:12:29,915
That's right.

202
00:12:29,982 --> 00:12:33,686
And it's even free, so why not?

203
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:38,891
Dad. God is here to save us.

204
00:12:40,459 --> 00:12:41,660
God is here...

205
00:12:43,662 --> 00:12:45,431
Okay, I'll do it.

206
00:12:45,664 --> 00:12:46,932
You can do the operation.

207
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,001
You'll have to get me better.

208
00:12:49,835 --> 00:12:53,506
I promise. I never fail.

209
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:57,676
Jesus, he said the line.

210
00:12:59,879 --> 00:13:01,447
Are you doing it for free?

211
00:13:01,514 --> 00:13:02,915
Hey, feel it.

212
00:13:05,384 --> 00:13:06,619
Why is it beating so fast?

213
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:07,853
It's fast, right?

214
00:13:08,187 --> 00:13:10,589
This could be
the greatest event in my life.

215
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,691
You're being shallow.

216
00:13:13,692 --> 00:13:15,795
The patient is Ichiro Gomi.

217
00:13:16,262 --> 00:13:17,963
Esophageal cancer, stage three.

218
00:13:18,264 --> 00:13:21,367
We plan subtotal esophagectomy...

219
00:13:22,201 --> 00:13:23,569
What?

220
00:13:25,204 --> 00:13:28,541
That's not something
worth showing live.

221
00:13:30,209 --> 00:13:34,213
I'll do pectoral muscle-sparing
esophagectomy with bowel rebuilt

222
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:37,082
in a speedier and more skillful way.

223
00:13:38,117 --> 00:13:39,285
Daimon.

224
00:13:40,619 --> 00:13:42,588
Watch your mouth.

225
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:48,427
Prof. Kusakabe has come
all the way from the United States.

226
00:13:50,029 --> 00:13:54,433
Pectoral muscle-sparing
esophagectomy?

227
00:13:55,601 --> 00:13:57,369
It's such a delicate surgery.

228
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:00,439
What if you fail?

229
00:14:00,773 --> 00:14:03,442
I never fail.

230
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:07,479
I understood.

231
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:14,353
Then I shall perform
VATS-E and HALS-G,

232
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:21,060
thoracoscopic esophagectomy
and gastric tube reconstruction by HALS.

233
00:14:21,227 --> 00:14:25,831
Of course, I will perform them
faster and more skillful than you.

234
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:34,473
VATS-E and HALS-G is
a cutting-edge technology.

235
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,109
It requires masterful technique.

236
00:14:38,177 --> 00:14:41,146
VATS-E is minimally invasive,
leaves very little scar,

237
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:43,616
and the recovery is quick.

238
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:47,152
HALS-G is a laparoscopic surgery

239
00:14:47,286 --> 00:14:49,788
which enables a left hand
to be inserted in the organ.

240
00:14:51,657 --> 00:14:55,261
I'm the one who never fails.

241
00:14:56,362 --> 00:14:58,998
That is wonderful,

242
00:14:59,298 --> 00:15:03,002
just what I expect
from Prof. Kusakabe.

243
00:15:03,969 --> 00:15:08,707
This is an operation worthy
of a live broadcast.

244
00:15:10,276 --> 00:15:12,177
All of you will learn a lot.

245
00:15:12,645 --> 00:15:15,381
Yes, sir.

246
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:21,553
Daimon, you should learn a lot
from Prof. Kusakabe.

247
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,525
Then try it.

248
00:15:26,859 --> 00:15:29,461
What's that arrogant attitude?

249
00:15:30,696 --> 00:15:31,530
Take her outside.

250
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:32,898
Yes, right away.

251
00:15:33,966 --> 00:15:38,971
Wait, wait. Don't go on your own.

252
00:15:39,038 --> 00:15:40,806
You're cheap, Daimon.

253
00:15:41,307 --> 00:15:43,609
Forgive us. She's so rude.

254
00:15:44,910 --> 00:15:46,045
That's alright.

255
00:15:46,145 --> 00:15:49,515
I like strong-spirited people like that.

256
00:15:50,349 --> 00:15:51,650
You're great.

257
00:15:51,817 --> 00:15:55,321
You have an open mind as I expected.

258
00:16:04,196 --> 00:16:06,799
All university hospitals in Japan
will see us.

259
00:16:06,865 --> 00:16:08,567
It's such a rare opportunity.

260
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:11,637
I'll be the cameraman.
I'll take good pictures.

261
00:16:14,073 --> 00:16:15,074
I'll help you dress.

262
00:16:16,175 --> 00:16:18,210
LISA HASHIMOTO, NURSE

263
00:16:18,277 --> 00:16:19,912
Kusakabe's assistant?

264
00:16:20,446 --> 00:16:22,948
I'm in charge of Mr. Gomi.

265
00:16:23,615 --> 00:16:26,118
Don't miss this chance.

266
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:31,290
I'd rather go to Massachusetts
as your wife.

267
00:16:36,929 --> 00:16:39,431
We're ready to broadcast.

268
00:16:39,565 --> 00:16:40,733
Okay, thanks.

269
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:46,305
The whole country will see
your ability as an executive manager.

270
00:16:48,707 --> 00:16:52,211
Yes. You're such a good-natured man.

271
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:57,449
You were a classmate
of Kusakabe's, right?

272
00:16:57,816 --> 00:17:01,220
Don't you feel jealous then?

273
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:07,092
Well, I'm proud to be his classmate.

274
00:17:09,995 --> 00:17:15,667
I would rather be admired
than be proud.

275
00:17:33,819 --> 00:17:36,989
Now we begin
thoracoscopic esophagectomy

276
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,792
and gastric tube rebuilt by HALS.

277
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:43,462
- I appreciate your hard work.
- Thanks.

278
00:17:44,997 --> 00:17:48,734
Blood pressure is in the 100's
and pulse is in the 60's. Normal.

279
00:17:53,305 --> 00:17:55,441
- Thanks.
- It's my pleasure.

280
00:17:58,544 --> 00:17:59,812
Scalpel.

281
00:18:06,652 --> 00:18:09,922
First, the incisions will be
made into five places

282
00:18:09,988 --> 00:18:12,024
on the right chest to insert port.

283
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:15,894
The usual posture is in
left lateral decubitus position,

284
00:18:16,295 --> 00:18:18,697
but Prof. Kusakabe chose
a prone position.

285
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:25,003
This posture is said to
improve the visual field

286
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:26,738
and the maneuverability.

287
00:18:43,255 --> 00:18:46,391
He's not bad.

288
00:18:48,994 --> 00:18:50,629
This meat croquette is good.

289
00:18:51,063 --> 00:18:53,565
- Avoid Greater omentum.
- Yes, sir.

290
00:18:56,368 --> 00:18:58,504
It's superb.

291
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:01,106
He's like a maestro.

292
00:19:01,173 --> 00:19:02,808
- Coagulation forceps.
- Yes.

293
00:19:03,408 --> 00:19:06,745
Coagulation of
left gastroepiploic artery.

294
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:14,520
It's like listening to an aria.

295
00:19:15,087 --> 00:19:16,855
I like the way you put it.

296
00:19:25,697 --> 00:19:26,698
Dad.

297
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:36,241
Proceed to esophagogastrostomy.

298
00:19:36,308 --> 00:19:37,776
Bring the stomach tube closer.

299
00:19:39,111 --> 00:19:40,712
Linear stapler.

300
00:19:46,718 --> 00:19:48,520
- Suction.
- Yes, sir.

301
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,570
Checking gastric tube
in the mediastinum.

302
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:32,397
Anastomosis complete.

303
00:20:32,464 --> 00:20:34,933
We'll start closing. Remove trocar.

304
00:20:36,535 --> 00:20:37,603
Stapler.

305
00:20:54,786 --> 00:20:56,655
Suture complete. Surgery complete.

306
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,191
Good job, sir.

307
00:21:19,511 --> 00:21:23,148
That was superb.
You all learned a lot, didn't you?

308
00:21:23,382 --> 00:21:25,117
- Yes.
- Let's applaud.

309
00:21:25,817 --> 00:21:26,718
Thank you.

310
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:35,560
Good job. Great team.

311
00:21:36,028 --> 00:21:37,663
That can only be an act of God.

312
00:21:37,996 --> 00:21:39,698
God is here.

313
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:46,505
Thank you. Thank you so much!

314
00:21:47,005 --> 00:21:48,307
Thank you so much.

315
00:21:50,008 --> 00:21:52,844
Good job. Great team.

316
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:56,381
Something's shady about him.

317
00:22:03,355 --> 00:22:08,126
Thanks for choosing me as
your anesthetist. I learned a lot.

318
00:22:08,527 --> 00:22:13,765
I always regard an anesthetist
as a maestro for surgeons.

319
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:18,103
Maestro?
A conductor of an orchestra?

320
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:19,237
Right.

321
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:22,741
We surgeons play the music

322
00:22:23,041 --> 00:22:25,310
by the batons of anesthetists.

323
00:22:26,211 --> 00:22:29,047
An anesthetist controls
the entire operation.

324
00:22:29,614 --> 00:22:32,050
I never thought of it that way.

325
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:35,320
You were such a brilliant maestro,

326
00:22:35,487 --> 00:22:37,622
or should I say, maestra.

327
00:22:38,290 --> 00:22:40,492
Thanks to you,
I could do a good job.

328
00:22:40,559 --> 00:22:43,328
- It's my pleasure.
- Observe Mr. Gomi.

329
00:22:43,895 --> 00:22:44,896
I will.

330
00:22:46,498 --> 00:22:48,700
If anything happen, call me.

331
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:50,202
Yes, sir.

332
00:22:50,736 --> 00:22:51,570
Good job.

333
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,942
Excuse me, Professor Kusakabe.

334
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:09,187
Oh!

335
00:23:10,522 --> 00:23:13,725
I'm going home, Maestra Jonouchi.

336
00:23:13,959 --> 00:23:16,528
- Were you listening?
- No, I wasn't.

337
00:23:22,167 --> 00:23:23,668
- I erased it.
- What?

338
00:23:26,438 --> 00:23:28,140
She heard the whole thing.

339
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:33,345
As they say, seeing is believing.

340
00:23:34,613 --> 00:23:35,480
Kondo.

341
00:23:35,614 --> 00:23:39,651
You learned a lot from Kusakabe's
operation today, didn't you?

342
00:23:39,718 --> 00:23:43,054
Yes. I was honored to
gain a valuable experience.

343
00:23:43,355 --> 00:23:45,490
Thanks, Prof. Kusakabe.

344
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:52,998
Kondo needs to
brush up his surgical skills.

345
00:23:53,064 --> 00:23:55,133
For my daughter's sake.

346
00:23:56,034 --> 00:23:57,202
For your daughter?

347
00:23:57,269 --> 00:24:03,175
This guy is trying to make
a pass at our precious daughter.

348
00:24:03,241 --> 00:24:06,311
He's a rude wicked wolf.

349
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:12,317
Don't put it that way.
It doesn't sound nice.

350
00:24:13,485 --> 00:24:19,191
But I think a man is dependable
when he has ambition.

351
00:24:20,992 --> 00:24:22,227
That's true.

352
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:24,262
Ready to eat?

353
00:24:24,529 --> 00:24:26,898
Yes. Thank you.

354
00:24:42,681 --> 00:24:45,750
- Serve me.
- Forgive me, sir.

355
00:24:48,186 --> 00:24:50,989
Speaking of ambition...

356
00:24:52,123 --> 00:24:55,927
The election
for the chairperson is coming up.

357
00:24:56,828 --> 00:25:01,132
I heard. Chairman Takano
was transferred, right?

358
00:25:01,266 --> 00:25:02,968
Yeah, he was transferred.

359
00:25:03,535 --> 00:25:08,240
So, the position became available
and we'll have an election.

360
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:12,611
In the old days, there were guys
with their ambition exposed

361
00:25:12,777 --> 00:25:14,446
trying to win the race.

362
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:18,717
But these days, everyone is quiet.

363
00:25:18,884 --> 00:25:22,354
They are so quiet
I don't know who to nominate.

364
00:25:24,256 --> 00:25:25,757
- Here, sir.
- Oh thank you.

365
00:25:27,959 --> 00:25:30,362
Ouch, it's hot. Ouch!

366
00:25:32,664 --> 00:25:34,900
- It's hot.
- I'm sorry.

367
00:25:35,834 --> 00:25:39,671
I appraise aspiration
more than ambition.

368
00:25:40,105 --> 00:25:42,240
You play an active role worldwide.

369
00:25:42,307 --> 00:25:44,609
I'm so impressed with your insight.

370
00:25:46,144 --> 00:25:47,078
Kusakabe.

371
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:50,582
If you could come to our hospital,

372
00:25:51,116 --> 00:25:54,986
I would make you
a chairperson right away.

373
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:56,655
Thank you very much.

374
00:25:58,056 --> 00:25:59,591
- Vegetables?
- Yes, please.

375
00:26:02,827 --> 00:26:04,863
- That's too small.
- There are many more.

376
00:26:09,367 --> 00:26:11,136
It's me. Excuse me.

377
00:26:11,369 --> 00:26:14,472
Could it be Marilyn
from Massachusetts?

378
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,809
- It's from Jonouchi.
- I see.

379
00:26:18,176 --> 00:26:20,845
Prof. Kusakabe, Mr. Gomi's condition
has taken a sudden turn.

380
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:22,647
What's his condition?

381
00:26:24,849 --> 00:26:28,019
Body temperature is 38. 2C
and the pulse is 120.

382
00:26:28,186 --> 00:26:29,721
He's having chest pain.

383
00:26:29,854 --> 00:26:32,357
It's usual after surgery.
Don't worry.

384
00:26:32,691 --> 00:26:34,626
- But...
- Let's wait and see.

385
00:26:36,828 --> 00:26:37,862
Understood.

386
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:48,873
Is everything okay?

387
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,343
Yeah. My surgery was perfect.

388
00:26:51,977 --> 00:26:55,046
The freelancer can't do
postoperative care.

389
00:26:56,247 --> 00:26:59,918
There can't be a mistake
with Genius Kusakabe.

390
00:27:02,787 --> 00:27:06,257
- Ebina, give me more meat.
- Yes, sir. Give me your bowl.

391
00:27:12,831 --> 00:27:13,832
Thanks.

392
00:27:25,844 --> 00:27:28,246
You'll feel better soon, Mr. Gomi.

393
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:29,447
Doctor.

394
00:27:29,514 --> 00:27:31,716
- Everything is fine.
- But...

395
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:39,424
Are you sure he's alright?
He's suffering more.

396
00:27:39,557 --> 00:27:42,027
Wasn't the surgery a failure?

397
00:27:42,293 --> 00:27:43,762
No. It went well.

398
00:27:50,802 --> 00:27:52,971
I see.

399
00:27:53,038 --> 00:27:54,606
Why are you reading a magic book?

400
00:27:54,773 --> 00:27:56,541
Are you switching jobs, Michiko?

401
00:27:57,208 --> 00:27:58,309
Here.

402
00:27:58,376 --> 00:28:01,179
What's this? Nothing's written.

403
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:04,949
I WON'T DO IT

404
00:28:06,451 --> 00:28:07,552
Oh my!

405
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:10,155
Here's the exposure.

406
00:28:13,058 --> 00:28:14,492
Oh, I've got it.

407
00:28:14,559 --> 00:28:19,064
Kusakabe is so slick in
what he says and what he does.

408
00:28:22,934 --> 00:28:24,536
Your cell does ring.

409
00:28:24,669 --> 00:28:28,039
A woman who's charmed
by the slick guy.

410
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:32,744
- Yes?
- Mr. Gomi's is worse.

411
00:28:33,111 --> 00:28:33,978
Worse?

412
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:36,448
His fever and pulse aren't going down.

413
00:28:36,948 --> 00:28:39,784
Prof. Kusakabe says
it's usual after surgery.

414
00:28:41,086 --> 00:28:43,321
There's something I'm concerned about.

415
00:28:43,688 --> 00:28:44,522
What?

416
00:28:45,590 --> 00:28:46,725
During the operation...

417
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,371
Where are you going?

418
00:29:13,685 --> 00:29:15,887
Antimicrobials calm him down.

419
00:29:16,721 --> 00:29:19,324
- How is it?
- It's perfect so far.

420
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:22,727
This is where it starts.

421
00:29:23,294 --> 00:29:25,230
Now the gastric tube
in the mediastinum.

422
00:29:34,973 --> 00:29:35,974
Go back.

423
00:29:39,077 --> 00:29:40,378
Now the gastric tube...

424
00:29:56,161 --> 00:29:57,295
That's what it is.

425
00:29:58,663 --> 00:29:59,898
You'll see tomorrow.

426
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:04,736
I think you were used
as an assistant for a magic show.

427
00:30:06,504 --> 00:30:07,438
Show it to me again.

428
00:30:13,077 --> 00:30:15,880
Prof. Kusakabe. Prof. Kusakabe.

429
00:30:17,515 --> 00:30:19,217
I'm taking the 4 o'clock flight back.

430
00:30:19,517 --> 00:30:21,386
My patients are waiting there.

431
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:23,955
These three days were fulfilling.

432
00:30:24,122 --> 00:30:27,959
Will you consider
reoperating on Mr. Gomi?

433
00:30:30,094 --> 00:30:31,329
Reoperation?

434
00:30:31,930 --> 00:30:35,066
If the result of the test requires it,

435
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:38,002
please extend your stay.

436
00:30:40,104 --> 00:30:42,507
Complications aren't unusual
after surgery.

437
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:46,477
I did my best
and succeeded in the operation.

438
00:30:47,312 --> 00:30:48,346
I was perfect.

439
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:51,549
Yes, but...

440
00:30:51,683 --> 00:30:53,151
I never fail.

441
00:30:57,655 --> 00:31:00,959
Jonouchi,
you are a brilliant anesthetist.

442
00:31:01,459 --> 00:31:05,263
I'd like to invite you
to the Massachusetts Medical School.

443
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:10,702
Think about it.

444
00:31:12,904 --> 00:31:13,905
I have to go.

445
00:31:34,158 --> 00:31:35,927
Suture leakage?

446
00:31:36,060 --> 00:31:39,631
Both the white blood cell
and CRP counts rose.

447
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:42,834
We detected an inflammation
in the mediastinum.

448
00:31:43,034 --> 00:31:45,803
But Kusakabe's suture was perfect.

449
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:50,174
I saw it close-by.
I've never seen such perfect suture.

450
00:31:50,441 --> 00:31:52,543
It was perfect.

451
00:31:53,278 --> 00:31:57,649
But, we see the color changes to black

452
00:31:58,683 --> 00:32:00,184
that spreads 3cm caudally.

453
00:32:01,019 --> 00:32:03,955
Gastric tube necrosis caused
by obstruction of blood. Look.

454
00:32:05,556 --> 00:32:06,858
EXAMINATION RESULT REPORT

455
00:32:07,725 --> 00:32:10,395
Necrosis has already started?

456
00:32:10,628 --> 00:32:13,932
Mr. Gomi will die from sepsis shock.

457
00:32:13,998 --> 00:32:17,635
- We need to reoperate immediately.
- No way.

458
00:32:17,835 --> 00:32:21,572
If we do that, people will think
Prof. Kusakabe failed.

459
00:32:21,739 --> 00:32:24,776
Consequently, it may harm Hiruma

460
00:32:24,976 --> 00:32:28,046
because he invited Kusakabe.

461
00:32:28,179 --> 00:32:30,548
- Who cares?
- We do.

462
00:32:31,316 --> 00:32:34,419
Care! It's the most important thing.

463
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:36,921
How could we tell the whole country

464
00:32:36,988 --> 00:32:41,025
about reoperating
after the one we did yesterday?

465
00:32:41,292 --> 00:32:43,194
You've got to be kidding!

466
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:47,065
If you insist on it,
do it secretly in 3 months.

467
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:50,902
Let's calm down, Office Manager.

468
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:52,570
Yes, sir.

469
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,772
Okay, okay. Listen, Office Manager.

470
00:32:54,839 --> 00:32:58,076
Complications after a surgery occur

471
00:32:58,142 --> 00:33:02,280
even when it's done
by a skilled physician.

472
00:33:02,347 --> 00:33:04,215
Sorry, I lost my composure.

473
00:33:05,016 --> 00:33:07,752
I understand how you feel.

474
00:33:08,219 --> 00:33:13,358
If you insist on reoperation,

475
00:33:13,458 --> 00:33:16,327
let's do it when it's a good time.

476
00:33:17,962 --> 00:33:19,297
You don't care if he dies?

477
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:31,576
- Executive Manager.
- Yes?

478
00:33:32,744 --> 00:33:36,014
Why don't we let Daimon reoperate?

479
00:33:40,284 --> 00:33:43,721
- What?
- Are you out of your mind?

480
00:33:47,825 --> 00:33:50,261
Why don't we let her do it
on one condition.

481
00:33:54,599 --> 00:33:55,433
Condition?

482
00:34:01,105 --> 00:34:04,542
Dad! Dad!

483
00:34:07,979 --> 00:34:11,049
Dad! Dad!

484
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:17,221
Dad! Dad!

485
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:19,724
Please wait here.

486
00:34:21,626 --> 00:34:23,694
Please help my dad! Don't kill him!

487
00:34:24,228 --> 00:34:25,930
Don't worry. I'll save him for sure.

488
00:34:26,631 --> 00:34:27,832
Really?

489
00:34:28,366 --> 00:34:29,801
I never fail.

490
00:34:30,034 --> 00:34:33,438
It's Ebina. We decided to reoperate.

491
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:37,742
- What?
- A mediocre saves a genius.

492
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:40,745
It's a nice change, once in a while.

493
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:44,882
Hey! Hey!

494
00:34:58,563 --> 00:35:00,665
Vitals are stable
under the general anesthesia.

495
00:35:01,032 --> 00:35:04,735
Blood pressure is 120/65,
heart rate is 95.

496
00:35:04,869 --> 00:35:07,338
Start urgent mediastinal drainage.

497
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:09,974
Forceps.

498
00:35:12,844 --> 00:35:14,011
Rib shear.

499
00:35:25,022 --> 00:35:27,658
Rinsing mediastinum. Saline water.

500
00:35:28,092 --> 00:35:29,427
Saturation level is dropping.

501
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:31,963
Adjusting anesthesia, but hurry.

502
00:35:33,464 --> 00:35:34,365
Don't worry.

503
00:35:39,303 --> 00:35:41,038
Lay the drain.

504
00:35:46,944 --> 00:35:52,517
This operation is performed
by you, Executive Manager.

505
00:35:56,854 --> 00:36:00,825
You will surpass "God's hands,"

506
00:36:01,926 --> 00:36:03,327
and you will become a new God.

507
00:36:04,595 --> 00:36:05,897
Then we will have...

508
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:10,968
even more outpatients.

509
00:36:12,136 --> 00:36:18,376
You have come up with
a terrible idea, Professor Ebina.

510
00:36:18,943 --> 00:36:20,044
Ebina,

511
00:36:21,579 --> 00:36:24,749
you think of such a cheap trick.

512
00:36:27,652 --> 00:36:32,290
But as your cheapness becomes excessive,

513
00:36:33,758 --> 00:36:35,092
it can be quite exhilarating.

514
00:36:37,828 --> 00:36:38,763
Thank you.

515
00:36:41,532 --> 00:36:43,367
Do a good job, Daimon.

516
00:36:50,107 --> 00:36:51,475
Why are you doing this?

517
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:54,879
Watch carefully, Kusakabe.

518
00:37:06,157 --> 00:37:08,726
Saturation level is 99%.
It's stable.

519
00:37:09,193 --> 00:37:11,229
Removing the necrotic gastric tube.

520
00:37:15,166 --> 00:37:17,902
Next, perform colon rebuild
with supercharge.

521
00:37:18,269 --> 00:37:19,337
Rebuild?

522
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:21,739
Not after inflammation subsides?

523
00:37:21,806 --> 00:37:26,310
We've been using antibiotics
before mediastinitis.

524
00:37:27,945 --> 00:37:29,780
Get ready to
change into supine position.

525
00:37:31,182 --> 00:37:32,149
Let's start.

526
00:37:34,285 --> 00:37:35,419
Scalpel.

527
00:37:36,387 --> 00:37:37,221
Forceps.

528
00:37:43,194 --> 00:37:45,963
That surgery needs to
be done in two stages.

529
00:37:46,597 --> 00:37:47,565
Right.

530
00:37:47,965 --> 00:37:51,302
The first operation is for drainage
and removal of necrosis.

531
00:37:52,136 --> 00:37:55,439
And a few months later,
a second will be for reconstruction.

532
00:37:58,209 --> 00:38:02,113
Then how can that woman
perform both at once?

533
00:38:06,017 --> 00:38:08,519
She's opposite to "God's hands."

534
00:38:10,821 --> 00:38:11,922
"Demon's hands."

535
00:38:14,892 --> 00:38:18,496
She is...the Devil.

536
00:38:30,941 --> 00:38:32,243
Hemorrhage?

537
00:38:32,543 --> 00:38:34,478
- 450 cc.
- How about from the drain?

538
00:38:34,612 --> 00:38:36,547
I'll keep an eye for any hemorrhage.

539
00:38:37,281 --> 00:38:38,182
Surgery completed.

540
00:38:48,459 --> 00:38:50,861
- Good job.
- Great job.

541
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:52,663
- Thanks.
- Good job.

542
00:39:12,083 --> 00:39:13,084
Kusakabe.

543
00:39:14,385 --> 00:39:19,757
We won't do anything
to harm your position.

544
00:39:23,661 --> 00:39:27,131
Have a safe trip back
to the United States.

545
00:39:51,522 --> 00:39:53,190
Are those syrup?

546
00:39:56,460 --> 00:39:58,329
After surgery, your brain dries up.

547
00:39:59,663 --> 00:40:02,900
If you feel that,
you perform true surgery.

548
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:05,002
Don't include me in your nonsense.

549
00:40:06,871 --> 00:40:08,105
It was a superb operation.

550
00:40:08,973 --> 00:40:13,177
I'll give you permission
to use the phrase, "I never fail."

551
00:40:13,544 --> 00:40:16,480
Are you still saying that?
You failed.

552
00:40:17,681 --> 00:40:21,085
Failed? My operation was perfect.

553
00:40:21,152 --> 00:40:23,821
You didn't cure the patient.

554
00:40:23,888 --> 00:40:26,657
That's why I'm saying you failed.

555
00:40:27,458 --> 00:40:30,694
Gomi suffered from mediastinitis
caused by suture leakage.

556
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:35,032
The suture was perfect.

557
00:40:35,166 --> 00:40:39,437
Yes. There was another reason
for suture leakage.

558
00:40:42,006 --> 00:40:43,140
During the surgery,

559
00:40:43,407 --> 00:40:48,446
you turned away
from the monitor for a second.

560
00:40:55,052 --> 00:41:00,424
You noticed the reconstructed
gastric tube started to cool,

561
00:41:00,491 --> 00:41:01,358
right?

562
00:41:02,827 --> 00:41:06,163
Vascular insufficiency caused
the suture leakage.

563
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:09,166
I know why you didn't point it out.

564
00:41:10,100 --> 00:41:11,068
Why?

565
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:15,105
You were scared, right?

566
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:17,475
You were scared of failing.

567
00:41:20,744 --> 00:41:24,715
There was a trick
to your phrase, "I never fail."

568
00:41:25,249 --> 00:41:26,350
Just like in a magic trick.

569
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:29,353
A trick?

570
00:41:29,553 --> 00:41:32,256
You never do anything you might fail at.

571
00:41:32,623 --> 00:41:33,524
That's your trick.

572
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:45,903
Please never use the phrase
"I never fail," any more.

573
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:48,572
It's a nuisance to me.

574
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:51,509
Prof. Kusakabe.

575
00:41:52,309 --> 00:41:55,312
I decline your invitation
to Massachusetts.

576
00:41:56,447 --> 00:41:58,082
I won't be your assistant...

577
00:41:59,450 --> 00:42:00,284
for your magic show.

578
00:42:05,589 --> 00:42:07,825
She stole my phrase, "I won't."

579
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:12,129
I'm leaving, too.

580
00:42:12,730 --> 00:42:16,100
You worked at
New York Cancer Center four years ago.

581
00:42:18,936 --> 00:42:21,372
The patient's name was Daniel Jack.

582
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:23,774
He was a famous singer.

583
00:42:24,975 --> 00:42:26,243
What are you talking about?

584
00:42:28,012 --> 00:42:29,446
You remember the disease.

585
00:42:30,614 --> 00:42:35,019
It's esophageal cancer,
stage four B,

586
00:42:35,619 --> 00:42:38,355
spreading to remote organs
such as lung and liver.

587
00:42:38,856 --> 00:42:42,026
In short, he was a patient
waiting for death.

588
00:42:44,261 --> 00:42:47,631
Of course, I gave up on him.

589
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:55,706
However, one surgeon
removed them perfectly

590
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:57,207
and cured him completely.

591
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:04,448
The surgeon's name was Dr. X.

592
00:43:05,849 --> 00:43:06,850
It's you, isn't it?

593
00:43:10,220 --> 00:43:11,956
I don't know
what you're talking about.

594
00:43:20,731 --> 00:43:21,865
Prof. Hiruma.

595
00:43:22,366 --> 00:43:27,438
Thank you for using both
Daimon and Jonouchi this time.

596
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:30,074
This is a melon. This is the bill.

597
00:43:38,882 --> 00:43:40,517
- Please take a look.
- Okay.

598
00:43:51,962 --> 00:43:57,434
What is this outrageous figure?

599
00:43:58,002 --> 00:44:01,472
We should get more than
what you paid to Prof. Kusakabe.

600
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:04,308
We had to work behind the stage.

601
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:09,380
I hear that patients around here

602
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:12,416
praise your "Buddha's hands,"

603
00:44:13,117 --> 00:44:16,020
as opposed to "God's hands."

604
00:44:17,688 --> 00:44:19,957
Buddha's hands? Really?

605
00:44:20,758 --> 00:44:22,426
Of course, both Daimon and Jonouchi

606
00:44:22,993 --> 00:44:27,164
will take your secret to their graves
with them.

607
00:44:27,965 --> 00:44:29,133
See you.

608
00:44:31,368 --> 00:44:32,269
Wait a second.

609
00:44:34,038 --> 00:44:34,905
Yes?

610
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:42,312
Next time, you bring me bills
for two people...

611
00:44:43,247 --> 00:44:44,081
Yes?

612
00:44:47,484 --> 00:44:49,019
Bring me two melons.

613
00:44:50,521 --> 00:44:53,624
I'm sorry. I didn't realize...

614
00:44:55,793 --> 00:44:56,760
I like melons.

615
00:45:00,631 --> 00:45:02,199
I like to eat a whole melon alone.

616
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:06,570
You should've gone to Massachusetts.

617
00:45:06,637 --> 00:45:07,838
You should've accepted it.

618
00:45:07,938 --> 00:45:09,073
Why?

619
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:12,342
You're the type who fits
in an organization.

620
00:45:12,643 --> 00:45:14,745
You don't have the skills

621
00:45:15,913 --> 00:45:18,649
to survive as a freelancer.

622
00:45:20,350 --> 00:45:23,954
Don't forget that I'm the maestra

623
00:45:24,021 --> 00:45:27,024
who conducts your operation.

624
00:45:27,658 --> 00:45:29,259
Without me,

625
00:45:29,326 --> 00:45:34,598
you probably can't keep saying
"I never fail."

626
00:45:34,765 --> 00:45:37,901
At your level,
you could also make a big mess.

627
00:45:40,537 --> 00:45:42,573
What!

628
00:45:43,140 --> 00:45:44,041
Be quiet.

629
00:45:44,174 --> 00:45:45,776
- What!
- Just hush! Be quiet.

630
00:45:45,843 --> 00:45:47,377
Be quiet.

631
00:45:47,745 --> 00:45:50,013
- I said be quiet.
- Why?

632
00:45:51,014 --> 00:45:53,484
<i>She hates groups, and being controlled.</i>

633
00:45:54,718 --> 00:45:59,389
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

634
00:46:02,326 --> 00:46:05,229
- Vital sign?
- Blood pressure at 100's. Heart rate 70's.

635
00:46:05,362 --> 00:46:06,363
Sinus.

636
00:46:09,266 --> 00:46:10,167
Scalpel.

637
00:46:11,902 --> 00:46:13,871
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

638
00:46:15,372 --> 00:46:17,808
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

639
00:46:20,844 --> 00:46:24,448
- His father.
- He has no desire to be promoted.

640
00:46:24,581 --> 00:46:25,916
You'll be a new hero.

641
00:46:26,049 --> 00:46:28,652
Affection towards the family?

642
00:46:28,786 --> 00:46:31,922
- I want my son to do it.
- Too late if it exploded.

643
00:46:31,989 --> 00:46:33,957
Knowing that it will explode?

644
00:46:34,091 --> 00:46:35,459
Every organ is necessary.
